31 more authors hold 6.7% together. The largest of them is Garrett Berg at 0.9%.

**Bus factor:** it is 1, meaning the smallest number of authors whose surviving lines reach 50% of the lines counted. Gallant alone passes that. Reaching 80% takes 2 authors. Both numbers cover all Rust files in the repo, which is 9 files.

**Identity merging:**
- Inès Moreau appears under 3 addresses: 120, 97 and 0 lines. I counted them as one person, but that is a guess from names and addresses. Unmerged, the largest single address has 120 lines (3.2%), which would put that person below Thiel at 74 only if the 97-line address were also separate. Nothing was written to `.mailmap`.
- Niv Kaminer and "nivkner" share one address, so they are counted as one person (45 lines).
- Ashley (68 lines) and Ashley Mannix (4 lines) may be the same person. This is a weak match, so I did not merge them. If they are one person, they hold 72 lines (1.9%).

**What the numbers leave out:**
- `src/ucd_tables.rs` is excluded as a generated file (647 lines).
- One bot is excluded (9 lines).
- Copy detection (`git blame -w -M -C`) is on. Without it, Gallant would hold 80.6%.
- The check for mechanical rewrites flagged one commit, `c584a1d` "style: switch to rustfmt" by Gallant. It touches 9 files, so it is a formatting change. I did not set it aside in the main numbers. With it set aside, Gallant has 2,830 lines (76.3%), so the picture barely changes.

These are surviving lines, not code quality or review work. Deleted code counts for nobody.
